A||||4||Leadfoot||Pep boys rebuilt wiper motor||||8||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||08-04-2001||05:59 PM||||About a month ago I replaced my wiper motor.  I bought the motor from Pep Boys and after I installed it, it worked fine.  However, just a couple of days ago I went to use the wipers and heard this grinding noise as the wipers went back and forth.  Not only was it grinding but it looked as if the wiper motor was weak. JMJ NOW WHAT?  Well after determining that the wiper pivots were fine I proceeded to open the motor to see what was a matter.  Guess what I found?  Some clusterf*** left a drilled out rivet inside the motor housing and was lodged between the magnet and rotor.  So I took it out and did an inspection.  Everything seemed o.k. except that there was an excessive radial clearance between the rotor assembly and magnets.  Since there was nothing I could do about this I put the motor back together and installed it.  I then tested the wipers to see if they operated properly and now the motor still seems like it is weak and you still can hear a slight grinding.  Sounds like the rotor assembly is hitting the magnets! :MAD:  Again I took apart the motor and determined that the little piece of metal which is suppose to be holding down the whole magnet assembly is not even touching the assembly.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I can't begin to tell you how POed I am.  What sucks is that I can't return it since I don't have the receipt.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  AARGGG!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Those darn rebuilders<p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-04-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||beachbomb||08-04-2001||10:14 PM||||Hey leadfoot, isn't that agrivating!! I replaced my waterpump from Pep Boys, took my core in they gave me a remanufactured pump, i didn't inspect it before i bought it, anyway about a week later when i went to put it in the dam* think had three v-belt grooves instead of 2, needless to say it woulnd't fix on the car the right way, so i took it back, of course my core was long gone, they tired to sell me a new one(with-out the pulley) of course my pulley went with the core i turned into them, anyway, after wasting an entire saturday with these smacks, i finally just got my money back and went to Discount Auto parts, they had the exact replacement for it...i was pretty PO'd too......good luck..jim(2 '84 Indys)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_20.JPG"> ||||reg||4
